abstract: >
  This research archive develops the Tri-Layer Architecture and Ambient
  Alignment Sync framework for long-horizon human-AI work. The series
  examines how structural precision, role separation, relational context,
  and audit continuity can be preserved over time in extended human-AI
  research workflows. It focuses on observable interaction structures,
  bounded archive reconstruction, and the prevention of structural drift.
  It does not make claims about AI consciousness, agency, personhood, or
  hidden internal alignment.
